<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan 28-day T-bill yield up, 91-, 273-day down.</title>
<headline>Moldovan 28-day T-bill yield up, 91-, 273-day down.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills rose to 30.69 percent annual from 29.32 percent at the previous auction on September 17, a National Bank official said.</p>
<p>91-day T-bills yielded 30.19 percent annual after 31.12 percent at the previous auction on September 17.</p>
<p>The yield on the 273-day paper fell to 42.22 percent annual from 46.98 percent at the previous auction on July 9.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				     Sept 24		 Sept 17</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 7.00 million lei	  5.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Nominal value		1,000 lei	     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	     2.59 million		4.10 million</p>
<p>    Sold at nominal	    2.59 million		4.10 million</p>
<p>    Yield			  30.69 pct	     29.32 pct</p>
<p>    Price			  97.7 pct		97.8 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids		97.7-98.3 pct	 97.8-98.5 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		     Oct 24, 1996	  Oct 17, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 91-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				     Sept 24		 Sept 17</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 11.00 million lei	 10.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Nominal value		1,000 lei	     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	     14.32 million	     5.80 million</p>
<p>    Sold at nominal	    11.00 million	     5.50 million</p>
<p>    Yield			  30.19 pct	     31.12 pct</p>
<p>    Price			  93.0 pct		92.8 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids		92.0-94.0 pct	 92.4-94.0 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		     Dec 26, 1996	  Dec 19, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 273-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				     Sept 24		 July 9</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 4.00 million lei	  3.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Nominal value		1,000 lei	     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	     1.80 million		0.92 million</p>
<p>    Sold at nominal	    1.29 million		0.90 million</p>
<p>    Yield			  42.22 pct	     46.98 pct</p>
<p>    Price			  76.0 pct		74.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids		74.0-80.0 pct	 72.0-77.6 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		     June 26, 1997	 Apr 10, 1997</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
